1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:06,037
Host: Welcome to KC desk note. Today we are unpacking one fresh research report and the question it raises.

2
00:00:06,397 --> 00:00:13,595
Host: NetEase just reported its first-quarter results for fiscal 2026, and the numbers came in well above expectations.

3
00:00:13,955 --> 00:00:21,618
Analyst: That’s right. Revenue grew 6% year on year to over 30 billion yuan, beating consensus by 4%.

4
00:00:21,978 --> 00:00:25,554
Host: And what really drove that beat? Was it a new game launch or something else?

5
00:00:25,914 --> 00:00:35,062
Analyst: Actually, it was the old reliable titles. PC games like the Fantasy Westward Journey series and Where Winds Meet showed impressive resilience.

6
00:00:35,422 --> 00:00:40,299
Host: So the existing portfolio is still performing strongly, even against a high base from last year.

7
00:00:40,659 --> 00:00:49,343
Analyst: Exactly. The PC version of Fantasy Westward Journey even hit a record high for peak concurrent users, at 3.9 million.

8
00:00:49,703 --> 00:00:54,533
Host: That’s a strong signal for the core business. But I also noticed the margin story was quite compelling.

9
00:00:54,893 --> 00:01:05,992
Analyst: Yes, gross margin expanded by over 5 percentage points to 69.4%. The gaming segment alone hit a record high of 74.8%.

10
00:01:06,352 --> 00:01:09,324
Host: That’s a huge jump. What explains such a big improvement?

11
00:01:09,684 --> 00:01:14,792
Analyst: It’s mostly a mix shift. Higher-margin PC titles took a larger share of revenue,

12
00:01:15,152 --> 00:01:20,400
Analyst: and the company also benefited from lower revenue-sharing fees charged by app stores.

13
00:01:20,760 --> 00:01:27,308
Host: So the profitability story is not just about revenue growth, but about how they’re making more from each dollar of sales.

14
00:01:27,668 --> 00:01:35,609
Analyst: Precisely. Non-GAAP operating profit rose 17% year on year, and the operating margin expanded to over 43%.

15
00:01:35,969 --> 00:01:42,099
Host: Now, the report also mentions an upcoming title called Sea of Remnants. What’s the significance there?

16
00:01:42,459 --> 00:01:51,190
Analyst: That’s a key catalyst for the second half of the year. It’s slated for a third-quarter launch, possibly as early as July to catch the summer gaming season.

17
00:01:51,550 --> 00:01:55,776
Host: So the market is looking at that as a potential re-acceleration point for gaming growth.

18
00:01:56,136 --> 00:02:02,591
Analyst: That’s the general expectation. But the report doesn’t settle the question of how big that title will actually be.

19
00:02:02,951 --> 00:02:07,270
Host: That’s a fair point. There’s always uncertainty around new game performance.

20
00:02:07,630 --> 00:02:14,271
Analyst: And there’s another open question. The company didn’t update on converting its Hong Kong shares to a primary listing.

21
00:02:14,631 --> 00:02:17,464
Host: That could be a meaningful corporate event down the line.

22
00:02:17,824 --> 00:02:23,536
Analyst: It is. But for now, the focus remains on the strong operational execution and the pipeline.

23
00:02:23,896 --> 00:02:29,747
Host: So for listeners who want the full picture, the report goes deeper into the numbers and the valuation framework.

24
00:02:30,107 --> 00:02:35,680
Analyst: Absolutely. There’s a lot more detail on segment performance and the sum-of-the-parts valuation.

25
00:02:36,040 --> 00:02:39,338
Host: And we’ll leave it there for now. Thanks for breaking that down.

26
00:02:39,698 --> 00:02:45,038
Analyst: My pleasure. Happy to continue the discussion in the community if anyone wants to dive deeper.
